      {
        "id": 86504,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-01-24T19:38:48.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Twice, but once was in error. (the error was advanced, and we timed something wrong)</p><p>When we did pull it off: &nbsp;(This Sunday)</p><p>(H) was 5, we had Fixer, Tempest, Scholar, Bunker and Wraith. &nbsp;Opening hands included Stratosphere, Reclaim and infared Eyepiece. &nbsp;So boom, drug to the bottom of the deck.</p><p>Scholar draws DDA, so Tempest and Scholar put Strat back in play round 2, and there were only three drugs in play. &nbsp;Two rounds later we got 4 victims in the safehouse and worked for four or five more rounds to get to all the drugs face down on the table, then we flipped him.</p><p>Second side Spite with 0 drugs face up isn't such a challenge, but once we realized we could do it, we had to try.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
