      {
        "id": 86509,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-02T15:23:26.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>We were on normal and got two drugs put on the bottom of his deck. in the first two turns.</p><p>We got 4 victims in the safehouse, so there were more victims than drugs face up &nbsp;(H) was 5, so 4 didn't flip. &nbsp;Start of turn there wasn't a fourth drug to flip face up, end of turn #3 got flipped face down.</p><p><span>Then with only 2 in play and both face-up the same would occur, none to flip up, one flips down.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>We had some come back out, due to shuffling, but they would get flipped down and sent back, and we just kept exactly 4 in the safehouse until we managed to get three drugs in play and all facedown. &nbsp;Then we flipped.</p><p>The other two drugs would have eventually come out of the deck, but that didn't happen for us.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 30,
        "post_type": 1,
