      {
        "id": 86516,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-03T01:13:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Christopher's response was that</p><p>1. &nbsp;a face down card has no text so it is not indestructible (unless granted that status by text which is readable)</p><p>2. &nbsp;A face down drug destroyed would go to the trash, but once it leaves the table it is no longer face-down, and it would gofrom the trash into play, where all the normal rules would effect it (except that it would now be face-up)</p><p>3. &nbsp;A face down drug can be stratosphered, but if played from the top of the deck goes right back into play with the other drugs.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>So the only way to get rid of a drug is to stratosphere then put it on the bottom of the villain deck. &nbsp;Although Spite shuffles enough that you can't bury any card for good.</p><p>The game we pulld it off a fourth drug came back into play when we fortunately had only 2 face-up, so it flipped face down.</p>",
        "post_number": 37,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:10:31.777Z",
